---
description: Mandatory IAQAR.AI project constitution
alwaysApply: true
---

Before making changes:

1. Read docs/PROJECT_CONSTITUTION.md.
2. Read docs/SYSTEM_ARCHITECTURE.md.
3. Read docs/IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md.
4. Do not contradict approved requirements.
5. Do not redesign the approved UI.
6. Preserve officeId isolation.
7. Do not invent missing business decisions.
8. Implement one approved phase at a time.
9. Run tests and build before reporting completion.
10. Do not claim untested integrations are working.

Additional binding rules:

- Never add a bottom navigation bar, a deals page («الصفقات»), a separate visible
  settings button, static demo operations, or unapproved home-page sections.
- Office Settings opens only by clicking the office logo or the office cover image.
- The visible office settings show: office name, broker name, license number, city,
  mobile number — never an email field.
- Every office-scoped Firestore document carries officeId; Firestore rules and the
  Cloudflare Worker both enforce tenant isolation — frontend hiding is never enough.
- Matching, operations, notifications, and cooperation records must be idempotent and
  deduplicated; never show internal lifecycle labels to brokers.
- WhatsApp/Telegram integrations are labeled honestly (adapter-ready / simulated vs
  production-connected); message drafts are broker-reviewed; never store fake delivery
  success.
- Record unclear requirements in docs/DECISIONS.md and stop instead of guessing.
